{"id": "2026-11-05-news-federal-council-proposes-disability-insurance-ov", "date": "2026-11-05", "stream": "news", "headline": "Federal Council proposes disability insurance overhaul", "summary": "The Federal Council proposed an AI/IV reform raising payroll contributions 0.2 points, tightening full-pension thresholds and adding an integration benefit for young adults; consultation to 4 Feb 2027.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/TS29TgaPkmw5", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "The Federal Council on Wednesday 4 November proposed a reform of disability insurance (AI/IV) that would raise payroll contributions by 0.2 percentage points, split between employees and employers, and opened a consultation that runs until Thursday 4 February 2027. The government says the insurance has run a structural deficit since the early 1990s: its pay-as-you-go deficit was over CHF 200 million in 2025 and could reach CHF 600 million in 2030, its fund now covers only 33% of a year's spending against a legal minimum of 50%, and without action it would be empty by 2031. The main new measure is an \"integration benefit\" for 18- to 24-year-olds, mostly with mental illnesses, who are not yet fit for vocational rehabilitation, an estimated 1,000 people a year or about a third of new pensions in that age group. Savings of CHF 150 million a year by 2030 would come partly from raising the disability degree needed for a full pension from 70% to 80% and cutting the daily allowance for people without dependants. On top of the permanent 0.2-point rise (about CHF 980 million in 2030), from 2030 to 2039 earnings above CHF 181,440 would pay an extra 0.6 points, and part of the casino tax would move from AHV/AVS to the disability insurance.", "why": "almost every payslip in Switzerland would carry a slightly higher deduction, and people with severe but not total disability would need a higher assessed degree to get a full pension.", "thread_id": "2026-11-05-news-federal-council-proposes-disability-insurance-ov", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-05", "event_date": "2026-11-04", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Federal Council", "AI/IV", "AHV/AVS"]}
{"id": "2026-11-05-news-switzerland-adopts-eu-s-21st-russia-sanctions", "date": "2026-11-05", "stream": "news", "headline": "Switzerland adopts EU's 21st Russia sanctions", "summary": "Switzerland adopted the EU's 21st sanctions package against Russia, adding 254 listings, 33 Russian banks and 41 shadow-fleet ships.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/KsmEWk4E-bHM", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Switzerland adopted the EU's 21st package of sanctions against Russia on Wednesday 4 November, with the new sanctions lists taking effect at 23:00 that day and the sectoral measures on Thursday 5 November. The EU adopted the package on Thursday 23 July 2026. Switzerland's version adds 254 people, companies and entities to its asset freeze, puts 41 more companies under tighter export controls and bans transactions with 33 Russian banks, 17 financial and crypto-asset firms, four Russian airports and two Russian ports, among others. It also adds 41 ships linked to Russia's \"shadow fleet\" (tankers used to move oil around sanctions) to a ban on buying, selling or servicing them. After what it calls a weighing of legal and foreign-policy interests, the Federal Council decided not to list two Russian nationals for now.", "why": "Switzerland is again following EU sanctions three and a half months after Brussels, which affects Swiss banks, traders and shippers dealing with Russia.", "thread_id": "2026-11-05-news-switzerland-adopts-eu-s-21st-russia-sanctions", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-05", "event_date": "2026-11-04", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Federal Council", "Russia", "EU"]}
{"id": "2026-11-05-news-auditors-fault-reserve-power-plant-plan", "date": "2026-11-05", "stream": "news", "headline": "Auditors fault reserve power plant plan", "summary": "The Swiss Federal Audit Office said significant savings were left unused in the CHF 2.3 billion plan for four reserve power plants for 2030-2045.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/pMuwRPRn2eWI", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The Swiss Federal Audit Office (SFAO/EFK) said on Wednesday 4 November that the federal government left \"significant savings\" unused when choosing and sizing the reserve power plants it plans for 2030–2045, which will cost CHF 2.3 billion. Electricity consumers would pay for the four plants through a surcharge on their bills; the Federal Office of Energy puts this at about CHF 10 per household, according to SRF. The SFAO found the purchase itself was mostly efficient. According to SRF, it estimates the savings at CHF 220 million, for example by using some of the more than 6,000 emergency generators already installed at hospitals and data centres. It also told SRF that the plants would not be needed if Switzerland meets its 2035 targets for renewable energy, and that whether to insure against slower growth is \"a political question\". The reserve plant at Birr (AG), built under emergency law for about CHF 500 million, had to be taken down this year after the Federal Administrative Court found that unlawful.", "why": "parliament will decide on a multi-billion bill that lands on every household's electricity tariff, and the auditors say it could be cheaper.", "thread_id": "2026-11-05-news-auditors-fault-reserve-power-plant-plan", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-05", "event_date": "2026-11-04", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Swiss Federal Audit Office", "Swiss Federal Office of Energy", "Swissgrid"]}
{"id": "2026-11-05-news-swiss-jobless-rate-holds-at-3-in-october", "date": "2026-11-05", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss jobless rate holds at 3% in October", "summary": "SECO said Swiss unemployment stayed at 3.0% in October 2026 with 141,015 registered unemployed, up 4.3% on a year earlier.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/UuA5YIwSJ2xh", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Swiss unemployment stayed at 3.0% in October, SECO said on Thursday 5 November, with 141,015 people registered as unemployed, 4.3% more than a year earlier. After seasonal adjustment the rate held at 3.1%, and the number of unemployed fell by 1,328 from September. Youth unemployment fell to 3.2%, while the rate for people aged 50 to 64 rose to 2.7%. The wider count of jobseekers rose by 2,409 to 230,001, or 4.9%.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-05-news-swiss-jobless-rate-holds-at-3-in-october", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-05", "event_date": "2026-11-05", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["SECO"]}
{"id": "2026-11-05-news-komyshuvakha-strike-toll-rises-to-42", "date": "2026-11-05", "stream": "news", "headline": "Komyshuvakha strike toll rises to 42", "summary": "The death toll from Russia's 2 November strike on an aid point in a Komyshuvakha underground school rose to 42 as Melania Trump hosted Russian and Ukrainian envoys ahead of Abu Dhabi talks on 10-11 November.", "url": "https://www.ukrinform.net/rubric-ato/4181666-death-toll-from-airstrike-on-komyshuvakha-rises-to-42-search-operations-continue.html", "source_domain": "ukrinform.net", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The death toll from Russia's air strike on Monday 2 November on an underground school in Komyshuvakha, in Ukraine's Zaporizhzhia region, has risen to 42, Ukraine's national police said on Thursday 5 November, and up to 33 people may still be under the rubble. According to Ukrinform, Russian forces dropped nine guided aerial bombs on the school while humanitarian aid was being handed out there; it was being used as an \"Invincibility Point\", one of the heated shelters where people can get power and help. Le Monde reports that Melania Trump is due to receive Russian and Ukrainian representatives at the White House on Thursday 5 November, including the two countries' human-rights ombudspeople, to discuss the local ceasefire she helped arrange for the evacuation of occupied Oleshky. Volodymyr Zelensky said that, after a call with US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner, Ukraine is preparing for three-way talks with the US and Russia in Abu Dhabi on Tuesday 10 and Wednesday 11 November.", "why": "a strike on a civilian aid point killed dozens days before the US-brokered talks, and Kyiv is using it to press allies for more air defence.", "thread_id": "2026-11-05-news-komyshuvakha-strike-toll-rises-to-42", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-05", "event_date": "2026-11-02", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Ukraine", "Russia", "Komyshuvakha", "Melania Trump", "Abu Dhabi"]}
{"id": "2026-11-05-news-new-bomb-threats-divert-flights-across-europe", "date": "2026-11-05", "stream": "news", "headline": "New bomb threats divert flights across Europe", "summary": "A second wave of bomb threats this week diverted or escorted flights across France, Italy, Austria, Bulgaria, Czechia and Belgium on 5 November.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/several-european-flights-receive-bomb-threats-some-divert/a-79861216", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["world", "security"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "A new wave of bomb threats against passenger flights disrupted air traffic across Europe on Thursday 5 November, two days after a similar wave on Tuesday 3 November that turned out to be hoaxes. An Aer Lingus A320 flying from Dublin to Rome was diverted under air-force escort to the Évreux military air base west of Paris and landed safely at 10:05, the French prime minister's office said. A Finnair flight from Helsinki was escorted by military jets to Rome Fiumicino, a Wizz Air flight from Milan to Warsaw diverted to Vienna, three Ryanair flights to Sofia landed under high alert (one diverted to Plovdiv), and Czech police prepared Prague airport for four landings after threats of explosive devices on board, while saying they assessed the threats' relevance as \"low\". No dangerous material had been reported found by late morning. DW notes that the threats coincide with apparent cyberattacks on supermarket freezers and French blood banks, but no link has been established.", "why": "even fake threats force fighter escorts and diversions across several countries, and European authorities are watching for a deliberate disruption campaign.", "thread_id": "2026-11-05-news-new-bomb-threats-divert-flights-across-europe", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-05", "event_date": "2026-11-05", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Aer Lingus", "Finnair", "Ryanair", "France", "Czechia"]}
{"id": "2026-11-05-news-finnish-court-jails-fitburg-crew-for-cable-sabot", "date": "2026-11-05", "stream": "news", "headline": "Finnish court jails Fitburg crew for cable sabotage", "summary": "The Helsinki District Court convicted the Fitburg's captain and boatswain of aggravated criminal damage for dragging an anchor across Gulf of Finland cables on 31 December 2025.", "url": "https://www.tuomioistuimet.fi/ajankohtaiset/karajaoikeus-on-antanut-tuomion-ns-fitburg-asiassa/", "source_domain": "tuomioistuimet.fi", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["new source"], "topics": ["geopolitics", "security"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The Helsinki District Court on Thursday 5 November convicted the captain and the boatswain of the cargo ship Fitburg of aggravated criminal damage for cutting undersea cables in the Gulf of Finland on Wednesday 31 December 2025, and sentenced them to three years and six months and two years and ten months in prison. The court found that the ship, which had left St Petersburg the day before, dragged its anchor along the seabed for several hours over about 130 kilometres outside Finnish waters, crossing nine telecom and power cables and a gas pipeline; two telecom cables were damaged. It found the anchor's locking mechanism worked, so the anchor must have been lowered after departure, and that both men must have known it was down. The court rejected the defence's challenge to Finnish jurisdiction because the effects of the deliberate crimes were felt in Finland, ordered both men taken into custody immediately and made them jointly liable for repair costs. According to DW, the captain is Russian and the boatswain Azerbaijani, and both denied wrongdoing.", "why": "a court has now ruled that dragging an anchor across Baltic cables was deliberate and can be tried in Finland, after a series of cable and pipeline incidents in the Baltic since Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine in 2022.", "thread_id": "2026-11-05-news-finnish-court-jails-fitburg-crew-for-cable-sabot", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-05", "event_date": "2026-11-05", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Fitburg", "Helsinki District Court", "Gulf of Finland", "Finland"]}
{"id": "2026-11-05-news-joshua-wong-gets-ten-more-years", "date": "2026-11-05", "stream": "news", "headline": "Joshua Wong gets ten more years", "summary": "Hong Kong's High Court sentenced Joshua Wong to ten more years for conspiring to collude with foreign forces, two months before his scheduled release.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/5/hong-kong-democracy-activist-joshua-wong-sentenced-to-10-years-in-jail", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["politics", "world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Hong Kong's High Court on Thursday 5 November sentenced pro-democracy activist Joshua Wong to ten more years in prison for conspiring to collude with foreign forces under the national security law, two months before he was due to be released in January 2027. Wong, now 30, has been in jail since December 2020 over the 2019 protests. He pleaded guilty in September to conspiring with the exiled activist Nathan Law and others to ask foreign governments and bodies to impose sanctions on Hong Kong and China. Judge William Tam said he started from 13 years and reduced it to ten for the guilty plea and mitigation, and that the sentence must express \"the community's abhorrence\" of the scheme. The US consulate in Hong Kong said it \"strongly condemns\" the sentence and called for his release, and Taiwan denounced \"endless political persecution\".", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-05-news-joshua-wong-gets-ten-more-years", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-05", "event_date": "2026-11-05", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Joshua Wong", "Hong Kong", "Nathan Law"]}
{"id": "2026-11-05-news-us-sanctions-iran-false-flag-shipping-network", "date": "2026-11-05", "stream": "news", "headline": "US sanctions Iran false-flag shipping network", "summary": "The US Treasury sanctioned an India-based network selling false flags to Iranian oil tankers and a Turkish firm serving sanctioned Iranian airlines.", "url": "https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/sb0681", "source_domain": "home.treasury.gov", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The US Treasury on Wednesday 4 November sanctioned an India-based network that it says sold false flags and fake ship certificates to tankers carrying Iranian oil, and a Turkish firm that serves sanctioned Iranian airlines. The Treasury says Suniel Kumar Sharma and his wife Jaspreet Preeti Shahid, based in Chandigarh, falsely claimed to represent the ship registries of countries including Guyana, Eswatini and Laos, using websites built to look like official registries, in a scheme it dates to at least 2014. Two other Indian nationals and nine linked entities were also listed, along with Turkey-based Fugo Ground Services, which the Treasury says handles flights of Iran Air Tour and Saha Airlines. The measures freeze any US assets and generally bar Americans from dealing with those listed. They are part of what the administration calls \"Operation Economic Outcast\", and Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said \"you are either with us or against us\".", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-05-news-us-sanctions-iran-false-flag-shipping-network", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-05", "event_date": "2026-11-04", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["US Treasury", "Iran", "India", "Turkey"]}
